cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Cognitive Offloading Adaptive Symbiosis
message: "If you use or discuss COAS, cite this repository and its author."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hudson
    given-names: Jupiter
    alias: WisdomLoveThePoet
repository-code: "https://github.com/jupiter8nohate/cognitive-offloading-adaptive-symbiosis"
url: "https://github.com/jupiter8nohate/cognitive-offloading-adaptive-symbiosis"
abstract: >-
  Cognitive Offloading Adaptive Symbiosis, abbreviated COAS, is a human-AI
  collaboration framework for reducing cognitive burden without transferring
  human authority over meaning, consent, identity, values, purpose, or final
  judgment. The project includes future-facing governance concepts for AGI and
  ASI while explicitly avoiding claims that its present software agents are AGI
  or ASI.
keywords:
  - Cognitive Offloading Adaptive Symbiosis
  - COAS
  - cognitive offloading
  - human-AI symbiosis
  - adaptive symbiosis
  - human agency
  - AGI governance
  - ASI governance
  - AI safety
  - cognitive sovereignty
